ed and they  are very well entrenched in the  psychology of the Indian people so that  is not  something we can just purchase jettison  or change so in the Security Council we  have you know stated that position very  clearly and we've made it very clear  that we do support the aspirations of  the Palestinian people for that  independent viable state but it should  of course exist in peace with Israel and  matters of this nature need to be solved  not through violence but through  dialogue mmm I'm a JK i'm from school of  planning in architecture bhopal i want  to ask that there was fun announcement  that there would be indo-us higher  education council would be established  for new institutions in india as you  know IITs and it's-- nsps etcetera have  been expanded for new institutions in  india will that council would have some  role indo-us higher education are  canceled well let's see for how the  summit proceeds we are just on the eve  of having the higher education summit  we'll have to see what the outcomes are  but the desire is to intensify  cooperation that will benefit higher  education institutions in india of the  sort that you mentioned to infuse more  you know know-how and experience that  comes from outside universities just  today when i was talking to the Yale  faculty earlier this evening the idea  that came to mind for instance is why  don't we have why can't we consider the  possibility of more tripartite or  trilateral consultations between India  China and the United States on these  issues because the Chinese have had a  long-standing collaboration with the  Americans from the days you know when  you look back at the founding of peking  university or the founding of ching hua  university or the founding of fudan  university you had American Americans  who came to establish those University  so there's been a very close linkage so  now that we are thinking of expanding  our linkages with the Americans in these  fields i think these three countries can  really build a future that will  be good for the for the university going  population in in all the three countries  another year student of the last  question yield student thank you first  we would like to thank you for coming  here and spending some good time with us  i'm at yale school of management  leadership and healthcare program and my  question to use their recent changes in  the health care policy going on apoorva  patel there are some recent changes  going on in healthcare policy within us  with the burgeoning cost and their  significant deficiencies in india and  healthcare market so could you please  elaborate little bit on how is there  some expedited initiative taken by  indian government to bring in healthcare  investment back in india and like some  other strategic value propositions that  you have for us I must be honest I'm not  an expert in that field so I won't be  able to answer that question with that  level of expertise that you perhaps  would want from from you know health  care expert but I spoke about  collaboration in development of drugs of  medicines we've set a set up a global  disease detection center now through a  bilateral mou between India and the  United States so we have started  consultations on how the two countries  can cooperate and do co-innovation as i  said in co development in dealing with  chronic disease detection treatment  development of new vaccines generic  drugs i spoke about in how US companies  and indian companies are doing excellent  work in this field so we need to  institutionalize this a little better we  need to see how we can provide more  funding there's not much funding that  comes from the United States for these  things at the moment and that perhaps is  understandable given the problems that  the economy faces here at this moment  but ideally we should be doing much more  in the public sector than even even in  the private sector the Green Revolution  in India happened because of the  fact